 "root_cause": "The nearest-frame search treated missing decoded timestamps as zero, and generation replaced them with the requested sampling target or zero. Nonfinite or out-of-range timestamps could reach conversion or produce generic failures rather than a precise unusable-anchor outcome.",
 "changes": [
  "Validate real decoded frame timestamps as finite numeric values within zero to 7200 seconds",
  "Reject missing, boolean, nonnumeric, nonfinite and out-of-range timestamps with media_frame_timestamp_unusable; huge integer conversion does not leak OverflowError",
  "Use the same validation in nearest-frame search and before image conversion for both metadata paths",
  "Remove target-time and zero fallbacks while preserving true zero, exact duration boundary and nearest-frame selection",
  "Keep known worker business failure reusable; no frame artifact or replay of the failed job"
 ],
